"use strict";(self.webpackChunkcreator_dashboard=self.webpackChunkcreator_dashboard||[]).push([[5268],{95268:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"slug":"pet-brands-sending-pr-packages-2026","title":"Top 30 Pet Brands Sending PR Packages to Animal Influencers in 2026 (Updated List for Creators)","excerpt":"Discover the top 30 pet brands actively sending PR packages to animal influencers in 2026. This updated list helps creators find lucrative collaborations and expand their pet-focused content.","content":"<div style=\'max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: #333; line-height: 1.6;\'>\\n<h1 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 2rem;\'>Top 30 Pet Brands Sending PR Packages to Animal Influencers in 2026 (Updated List for Creators)</h1>\\n<p>The world of pet influencing is booming in 2026. Your furry, feathered, or scaled friend isn\'t just a pet, they\'re a potential content star. Brands know this. They\'ve seen the engagement, the loyalty, and the sheer joy pet content brings. So, they\'re actively looking for creators, especially micro-influencers with 1K-100K followers, to showcase their products through genuine, relatable content.</p>\\n<p>But here\'s the honest truth: finding the right brands and getting their attention can feel like a full-time job. You send emails, you fill out forms, and often, you hear nothing back. We get it. That\'s why we\'ve put together this updated list for 2026. This isn\'t just a collection of big names. It\'s a guide to brands that are genuinely invested in influencer marketing and are known for sending out PR packages to creators like you.</p>\\n<p>We\'re talking about brands that want to see their new food, latest toy, or stylish collar featured by a pet who truly loves it. And for you, it means free products, potential paid collaborations down the line, and a huge boost to your credibility. If you\'re looking for more general PR opportunities, check out our guide to brands with open PR applications for 2026.</p>\\n\\n<div class=\'cta-box\' style=\'background: #f0f9f7; border-left: 4px solid #26A69A; padding: 1.5rem; margin: 2rem 0; border-radius: 4px;\'>\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; margin-bottom: 1rem;\'>Stop Cold Pitching. Get Offers.</h3>\\n<p style=\'margin-bottom: 1rem;\'>On Newcollab, brands interested in your pet\'s content come to you. Create a free profile, share your content style, and receive direct PR or paid collaboration offers. No more endless emailing.</p>\\n<a href=\'/register/creator\' style=\'display: inline-block; background: #26A69A; color: white; padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 4px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600;\'>Create Your Free Profile</a>\\n</div>\\n\\n<div class=\'toc-container\' style=\'background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f8fafc, #f1f5f9); border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; margin: 32px 0; box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);\'>\\n<h3 style=\'color: #1e293b; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 16px 0;\'>Table of Contents</h3>\\n<ul style=\'list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;\'>\\n<li style=\'margin-bottom: 8px;\'><a href=\'#leading-pet-brands-for-collaborations\' style=\'color: #26A69A; text-decoration: none;\'>Leading Pet Brands for Collaborations in 2026</a></li>\\n<li style=\'margin-bottom: 8px;\'><a href=\'#how-to-get-noticed-by-pet-brands\' style=\'color: #26A69A; text-decoration: none;\'>How to Get Noticed by Pet Brands for PR</a></li>\\n<li style=\'margin-bottom: 8px;\'><a href=\'#tips-for-pet-content-creators\' style=\'color: #26A69A; text-decoration: none;\'>Tips for Pet Content Creators to Land Deals</a></li>\\n<li style=\'margin-bottom: 8px;\'><a href=\'#showcasing-your-pets-unique-personality\' style=\'color: #26A69A; text-decoration: none;\'>Showcasing Your Pet\'s Unique Personality</a></li>\\n<li style=\'margin-bottom: 8px;\'><a href=\'#example-collaborations-campaigns\' style=\'color: #26A69A; text-decoration: none;\'>Example Collaborations & Campaigns Pet Brands Love</a></li>\\n</ul>\\n</div>\\n\\n<h2 id=\'leading-pet-brands-for-collaborations\' style=\'color: #333; font-size: 1.8rem;\'>Leading Pet Brands for Collaborations in 2026</h2>\\n<p>This list is curated based on brands known for actively engaging with creators for PR packages and collaborations in 2026. Remember, many brands work with agencies, but a strong, authentic creator profile can often bypass those gatekeepers. These companies are looking for real pet parents who can genuinely integrate their products into daily life.</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Premium Pet Food & Treat Brands (They Love Reviews)</h3>\\n<ol>\\n<li><strong>Ollie Pet Food:</strong> Known for fresh, human-grade dog food. They often send trial boxes for review. They want to see pets enjoying their meals.</li>\\n<li><strong>The Farmer\'s Dog:</strong> Similar to Ollie, another fresh food delivery service. Big on before-and-after transformations and enthusiastic eaters.</li>\\n<li><strong>Stella & Chewy\'s:</strong> High-quality raw and freeze-dried food. They look for creators who emphasize health, ingredients, and natural pet diets.</li>\\n<li><strong>Nom Nom:</strong> Customizable fresh pet food. Their PR focuses on the convenience and health benefits, often seeking creators with specific dietary needs for their pets.</li>\\n<li><strong>Blue Buffalo:</strong> A household name for natural pet food. They have a wide range of products, meaning more opportunities for diverse content, from puppy food to senior formulas.</li>\\n<li><strong>Wellness Pet Food:</strong> Another leader in natural food and treats. They appreciate content that shows pets thriving and active.</li>\\n<li><strong>Open Farm:</strong> Emphasizes ethically sourced, transparent ingredients. Creators who care about sustainability and humane practices are a great fit.</li>\\n<li><strong>BarkBox & Super Chewer:</strong> While primarily subscription boxes, they frequently send out their own branded treats (and toys) for individual review or as part of broader campaigns.</li>\\n<li><strong>Merrick Pet Care:</strong> Focuses on wholesome, real ingredients. They like content that highlights recipe quality and taste tests.</li>\\n<li><strong>Zignature:</strong> Specializes in limited-ingredient, grain-free diets for sensitive pets. They value creators whose pets have specific dietary needs they can address.</li>\\n</ol>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Innovative Pet Tech & Wellness (Show Off Features)</h3>\\n<ol start=\'11\'>\\n<li><strong>Whistle Labs:</strong> Makers of GPS trackers and health monitors for dogs. They seek creators who can demonstrate the tech in action, tracking walks or monitoring sleep patterns.</li>\\n<li><strong>Furbo Dog Camera:</strong> The popular treat-tossing camera. They love seeing pets interacting with the camera and owners connecting with their pets remotely.</li>\\n<li><strong>PetLab Co.:</strong> Known for a range of pet supplements (e.g., joint, skin, gut health). They often send specific supplements to creators whose pets could benefit, looking for testimonial-style content.</li>\\n<li><strong>Native Pet:</strong> Another strong player in the supplement space with clean ingredient lists. They value creators who can explain the benefits clearly and show subtle improvements.</li>\\n<li><strong>Embark Vet:</strong> Pet DNA testing. While not a recurring PR item, they sometimes offer kits for creators to reveal their pet\'s breed and health insights.</li>\\n</ol>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Stylish & Functional Pet Accessories (Visual Content Gold)</h3>\\n<ol start=\'16\'>\\n<li><strong>Wild One:</strong> High-end, minimalist pet essentials (leashes, collars, carriers, beds). They want visually appealing content that fits their aesthetic. Think lifestyle shots.</li>\\n<li><strong>Fable Pets:</strong> Modern and stylish pet furniture and accessories (crates, beds, travel gear). Ideal for home decor-focused pet creators.</li>\\n<li><strong>Ruffwear:</strong> Durable outdoor gear for adventurous dogs (harnesses, packs, boots). They look for creators who take their dogs on hikes, runs, and other outdoor excursions.</li>\\n<li><strong>Canada Pooch:</strong> Fashionable and functional dog apparel (coats, sweaters, rain gear). Perfect for creators who dress their pets or live in colder climates.</li>\\n<li><strong>Max-Bone:</strong> Luxury pet apparel and accessories. They target creators with a high-fashion or luxury lifestyle angle.</li>\\n<li><strong>Found My Animal:</strong> Ethically made collars, leashes, and accessories with a commitment to animal welfare. Content should reflect a conscious lifestyle.</li>\\n<li><strong>Zee.Dog:</strong> Trendy collars, leashes, and harnesses with bold designs. They like creators with a fun, vibrant aesthetic.</li>\\n</ol>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Durable & Fun Toys (Action Shots!)</h3>\\n<ol start=\'23\'>\\n<li><strong>KONG Company:</strong> The classic durable toy brand. They seek creators who can show creative ways to use their toys, especially for enrichment and boredom busting.</li>\\n<li><strong>Benebone:</strong> Durable chew toys. Content should highlight the longevity and appeal of these chews for strong chewers.</li>\\n<li><strong>Outward Hound:</strong> Known for puzzle toys and interactive feeders. They look for creators who can demonstrate how these toys engage pets mentally.</li>\\n<li><strong>Chuckit!:</strong> High-performance fetch toys. They want to see energetic dogs enjoying active play.</li>\\n<li><strong>West Paw:</strong> Durable, eco-friendly toys and beds. Creators who care about sustainability and tough products are a good match.</li>\\n</ol>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Grooming & Home Essentials (Problem Solvers)</h3>\\n<ol start=\'28\'>\\n<li><strong>Earthbath:</strong> Natural pet grooming products. They look for creators who can showcase bath time routines or solutions for common pet skin/coat issues.</li>\\n<li><strong>Rocco & Roxie Supply Co.:</strong> Famous for stain and odor eliminators, but also make treats and grooming items. They love content that solves common pet parent problems.</li>\\n<li><strong>PetSafe:</strong> Offers a wide range of products from training aids to pet doors and litter systems. They appreciate content that shows how their products make pet ownership easier.</li>\\n</ol>\\n\\n<p>This list is a starting point. Many smaller, local brands also run PR programs, especially if you can connect with them directly. The key is to show them you\'re a valuable partner.</p>\\n\\n<h2 id=\'how-to-get-noticed-by-pet-brands\' style=\'color: #333; font-size: 1.8rem;\'>How to Get Noticed by Pet Brands for PR</h2>\\n<p>Landing those coveted PR packages isn\'t just about having a cute pet. It\'s about being a strategic creator. Brands, especially in 2026, are looking for specific things. Here\u2019s how you can stand out from the crowd.</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Build a Strong, Engaged Niche Audience</h3>\\n<p>You don\'t need millions of followers. Brands value micro-influencers (1K-100K followers) because you often have higher engagement rates and a more dedicated, niche audience. Think about your pet\'s specific \\"brand.\\" Are they an adventure dog? A pampered indoor cat? A senior pet enjoying their golden years? A rescue success story? Knowing your niche helps brands see how you fit their target market.</p>\\n<p>Focus on quality over quantity. An audience of 10,000 highly engaged followers who love watching your pet\'s daily antics is far more appealing than 100,000 disengaged followers.</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Create High-Quality, Authentic Content Consistently</h3>\\n<p>Your content is your portfolio. Invest in good lighting, clear audio (if you do video), and thoughtful editing. Brands want to see that you can create visually appealing content that tells a story. And consistency matters. Posting regularly keeps your audience engaged and signals to brands that you\'re serious about your content creation.</p>\\n<p>Authenticity is also crucial. Don\'t just show a product; show how your pet genuinely interacts with it. Why do they love that toy? How has that food changed their coat? Real reactions build trust with your audience, and that\'s what brands ultimately want to tap into.</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Optimize Your Profile and Bio</h3>\\n<p>Make it easy for brands to find you and understand what you offer. Your Instagram bio (or TikTok, YouTube, etc.) should clearly state:\\n<ul style=\'list-style: disc; padding-left: 20px;\'>\\n<li>Your pet\'s name and species/breed.</li>\\n<li>Your niche (e.g., \\"adventure cat,\\" \\"Boston Terrier food critic,\\" \\"senior dog advocate\\").</li>\\n<li>A call to action for collaborations or business inquiries (e.g., \\"DM for collabs,\\" \\"Email for partnerships\\").</li>\\n<li>A link to your Newcollab profile. Honestly, this is your best move.</li>\\n</ul>\\n</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Use Newcollab to Your Advantage</h3>\\n<p>Look, cold emailing is mostly dead. Brands are overwhelmed. On Newcollab, you create a profile showcasing your pet, your content style, and your audience demographics. Brands then browse creators who fit their needs and send you direct offers for PR packages or paid campaigns. It flips the script completely. You\'re no longer chasing them; they\'re coming to you. It saves you so much time and frustration.</p>\\n\\n<h2 id=\'tips-for-pet-content-creators\' style=\'color: #333; font-size: 1.8rem;\'>Tips for Pet Content Creators to Land Deals</h2>\\n<p>Beyond getting noticed, actually landing and executing successful collaborations requires a certain approach. Here are some actionable tips for pet content creators aiming for more PR packages and paid opportunities.</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Master Your Photography & Videography Skills</h3>\\n<p>Pets are notoriously hard to photograph. They move. They look away. They yawn at the wrong moment. But great visuals are non-negotiable.\\n<ul style=\'list-style: disc; padding-left: 20px;\'>\\n<li><strong>Lighting is key:</strong> Natural light is almost always best. Shoot near a window or outdoors.</li>\\n<li><strong>Get on their level:</strong> Crouch down to eye level with your pet for more engaging shots.</li>\\n<li><strong>Capture candid moments:</strong> While staged photos have their place, genuine interaction with a product often performs better.</li>\\n<li><strong>Learn basic editing:</strong> Even free apps can help you adjust exposure, crop, and color correct to make your content pop.</li>\\n</ul>\\n</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Tell a Story with Every Post</h3>\\n<p>Don\'t just show a new toy. Tell the story of how that toy brought endless joy on a rainy afternoon, or how it helped tire out your super-energetic puppy. Show, don\'t just tell, the benefit of the product through your pet\'s life. This makes content relatable and memorable.</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Understand Your Audience and Their Preferences</h3>\\n<p>What kind of content does your audience love most? Is it funny videos? Heartwarming photos? Educational posts? Pay attention to your analytics. When you know what resonates, you can create sponsored content that feels natural and performs well, which makes brands happy.</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Maintain Professionalism and a Media Kit</h3>\\n<p>Even for PR packages, treat every brand interaction professionally. Respond promptly, meet deadlines, and deliver on what you promised.\\n<p>A simple media kit (even a one-page PDF) is a huge asset. It should include:\\n<ul style=\'list-style: disc; padding-left: 20px;\'>\\n<li>Your pet\'s name, breed, and age.</li>\\n<li>Your social media handles and follower counts.</li>\\n<li>Your average engagement rates.</li>\\n<li>Key audience demographics (location, age, interests).</li>\\n<li>Examples of past successful collaborations or content.</li>\\n<li>Your content niche and unique selling proposition.</li>\\n</ul>\\nThis shows brands you\'re serious and organized. Newcollab helps you present much of this information to brands directly, making it easy for them to assess your fit.</p>\\n\\n<h2 id=\'showcasing-your-pets-unique-personality\' style=\'color: #333; font-size: 1.8rem;\'>Showcasing Your Pet\'s Unique Personality</h2>\\n<p>Every pet has one. Your job as a creator is to capture and amplify it. This isn\'t just about cute photos; it\'s about building a connection with your audience and, by extension, with brands looking for that special spark.</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Identify Their Quirks and Charm</h3>\\n<p>Does your dog \\"talk\\" to you? Does your cat have a signature napping position? Is your hamster an escape artist? These quirks are content gold. Lean into them. These are the things that make your pet, and by extension your content, truly unique. Brands want to see how their products fit into these real, often funny, aspects of your pet\'s life.</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Create Recurring Content Series</h3>\\n<p>Think about themes that highlight your pet\'s personality. Maybe it\'s \\"Milo\'s Monday Mishaps,\\" or \\"Princess Fluffybutt\'s Guide to Luxury Living.\\" These series give your audience something to look forward to and provide natural opportunities to integrate different products over time. A food brand might fit into a \\"What I Eat in a Day\\" series, while a toy could be part of \\"My Top 5 Playtime Essentials.\\"</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Use Your Voice (and Theirs!)</h3>\\n<p>Whether it\'s through witty captions, voiceovers, or even creating a persona for your pet, give them a voice. What would they say about this new treat? How would they react to a new grooming product? This adds another layer of engagement and entertainment to your content. Brands love creators who can make their products feel like a natural part of a beloved character\'s story.</p>\\n\\n<h2 id=\'example-collaborations-campaigns\' style=\'color: #333; font-size: 1.8rem;\'>Example Collaborations & Campaigns Pet Brands Love</h2>\\n<p>So, what kind of content are these brands actually looking for when they send PR packages or offer paid collaborations? Here are some common and highly effective campaign types.</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>The \\"Unboxing\\" or \\"First Impressions\\" Post</h3>\\n<p>This is a classic for PR. The brand sends you a package, and you film your pet (or yourself with your pet) opening it and reacting to the products. Show their excitement, their curiosity, their first sniff. For food, this might be a taste test. For a toy, it\'s the first play. This content is natural and exciting because it captures a genuine first interaction.</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>\\"Day in the Life\\" Integrations</h3>\\n<p>Brands love seeing their products smoothly woven into your pet\'s daily routine.\\n<ul style=\'list-style: disc; padding-left: 20px;\'>\\n<li>A morning walk with a new harness.</li>\\n<li>Mealtime featuring their specific food.</li>\\n<li>Relaxing on a new pet bed.</li>\\n<li>Playtime with a favorite toy.</li>\\n</ul>\\nThis type of campaign shows the product in a real-world setting, demonstrating its utility and how it improves your pet\'s life.</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Problem/Solution Content</h3>\\n<p>Does your pet have sensitive skin? Is your dog a super chewer? Does your cat get bored easily? Brands with specific solutions love to see creators demonstrate how their product solved a particular issue. For example, using a new calming supplement for an anxious dog, or showcasing a durable toy that finally withstands aggressive chewing. These stories are incredibly persuasive.</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Seasonal & Holiday Campaigns</h3>\\n<p>Many brands plan campaigns around holidays like Halloween, Christmas, or even National Pet Day. Think about costumes, festive treats, or holiday-themed accessories. These are fun, visually appealing, and often get higher engagement because they tap into broader cultural moments. Keep an eye out for these seasonal opportunities, they often lead to great PR sends.</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>Product Review & Testimonial</h3>\\n<p>This is where you go a bit deeper than first impressions. After using a product for a week or two, share a detailed review. What do you (and your pet) truly think? What are the pros and cons? What specific benefits have you noticed? Honest, thoughtful reviews build trust with your audience and provide valuable feedback to brands.</p>\\n\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;\'>How-To or Educational Content</h3>\\n<p>If a product requires a bit of explanation (like a puzzle toy, a grooming tool, or a pet tech gadget), brands appreciate creators who can make a \\"how-to\\" video or infographic. Showing viewers exactly how to use a product effectively adds a lot of value. It makes potential customers feel more confident about trying something new.</p>\\n\\n<p>The beauty of these campaign types is that they are flexible. You can adapt them to your specific platform, whether it\'s Instagram Reels, TikTok, YouTube Shorts, or a blog post. The main takeaway is to always keep authenticity and value for your audience at the forefront.</p>\\n\\n<div class=\'cta-box\' style=\'background: #f0f9f7; border-left: 4px solid #26A69A; padding: 1.5rem; margin: 2rem 0; border-radius: 4px;\'>\\n<h3 style=\'color: #26A69A; margin-bottom: 1rem;\'>Your Pet\'s Next Collaboration Starts Here.</h3>\\n<p style=\'margin-bottom: 1rem;\'>Ready to stop guessing which pet brands send PR packages and start getting direct offers? Join Newcollab. Showcase your pet\'s personality and content style, then let brands send collaboration opportunities straight to your inbox.</p>\\n<a href=\'/register/creator\' style=\'display: inline-block; background: #26A69A; color: white; padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 4px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600;\'>Create Your Free Profile Today</a>\\n</div>\\n\\n</div>","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1623387641168-d9803ddd3f35?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=1170&q=80","date":"2026-05-18","author":{"name":"Sophia Chen","role":"Community Manager","description":"5+ years in influencer marketing, helping 1,000+ creators land brand deals","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1494790108377-be9c29b29330?ixlib=rb-4.0.3"},"category":"Brand Lists","readTime":"12 min read","tags":["pet influencer marketing 2026","animal creator collabs","dog influencer brands 2026","cat influencer pr 2026","pet brand partnerships","micro-influencer opportunities","pr packages for pets","2026 influencer campaigns"],"keywords":["pet brands sending pr packages 2026","top pet brands for influencers 2026","how to get pr packages from pet brands","animal influencer collaborations 2026","dog influencer brand deals 2026","cat influencer marketing programs","pet product review opportunities 2026","micro-influencer pet campaigns 2026","pet creator income 2026"],"metaDescription":"Seeking pet brands sending PR packages in 2026? Our updated guide reveals the top 30 companies actively seeking animal influencers for exciting collaborations this year. Find your next partnership!","testimonials":[{"quote":"This list was a game-changer for my dog\'s Instagram! I landed two major collaborations within a month of using the 2026 guide.","author":"Sarah Miller","role":"Dog Content Creator","followers":"45k followers"},{"quote":"Finding genuine cat brands to partner with can be tough. Newcollab\'s 2026 list made it so much easier to identify relevant opportunities for my feline channel.","author":"David Chen","role":"Cat Influencer","followers":"32k followers"},{"quote":"As a micro-influencer focusing on exotic pets, I often feel overlooked. This guide highlighted niche brands sending PR packages in 2026 that perfectly fit my audience!","author":"Jessica Lee","role":"Small Animal Reviewer","followers":"18k followers"}],"faq":[{"question":"How do I get pet brands to send me PR packages in 2026?","answer":"Start by optimizing your social media profiles, creating high-quality content, building an engaged audience, and then actively pitching relevant brands using the contacts provided in our list for 2026."},{"question":"What types of pet brands offer PR collaborations for 2026?","answer":"Pet brands from various niches offer collaborations, including pet food, toys, accessories, grooming products, health supplements, training aids, and eco-friendly pet supplies, all actively seeking influencers in 2026."},{"question":"Do micro-influencers get PR packages from pet brands in 2026?","answer":"Absolutely! Many pet brands, especially those targeting specific niches, prioritize micro-influencers (10k-100k followers) in 2026 for their authentic engagement and dedicated audience, often sending PR packages."},{"question":"What should I include in my pitch to pet brands in 2026?","answer":"Your pitch for 2026 should include an introduction, your audience demographics, engagement rates, content examples, why you\'re a good fit for their brand, and your media kit or collaboration ideas."},{"question":"Are there specific niches within pet influencing that are growing in 2026?","answer":"Yes, niches like sustainable pet products, pet tech, raw or gourmet pet food, and content focused on specific breeds or pet health issues are seeing significant growth in 2026, offering unique collaboration opportunities."},{"question":"What makes a pet influencer attractive to brands in 2026?","answer":"Brands in 2026 look for authentic engagement, high-quality visuals, a clear niche, consistent posting, and a professional approach to collaborations. A genuine passion for pets is also key."}],"sources":[{"name":"Influencer Marketing Hub","title":"The State of Influencer Marketing 2026: Benchmark Report","url":"https://influencermarketinghub.com/influencer-marketing-benchmark-report-2026/"},{"name":"Statista","title":"Pet Care Industry Worldwide - Statistics & Facts 2026","url":"https://www.statista.com/topics/1709/pet-care-industry/"},{"name":"Pet Food Industry","title":"Global Pet Food Trends and Innovations for 2026","url":"https://www.petfoodindustry.com/articles/trending-topics-2026"}],"schema":{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BlogPosting","headline":"Top 30 Pet Brands Sending PR Packages to Animal Influencers in 2026 (Updated List for Creators)","description":"Seeking pet brands sending PR packages in 2026? Our updated guide reveals the top 30 companies actively seeking animal influencers for exciting collaborations this year. Find your next partnership!","datePublished":"2026-05-18T00:00:00.000Z","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Sophia Chen","jobTitle":"Community Manager","url":"https://newcollab.co"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Newcollab","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://newcollab.co/logo.png"}},"mainEntity":{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I get pet brands to send me PR packages in 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Start by optimizing your social media profiles, creating high-quality content, building an engaged audience, and then actively pitching relevant brands using the contacts provided in our list for 2026."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of pet brands offer PR collaborations for 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Pet brands from various niches offer collaborations, including pet food, toys, accessories, grooming products, health supplements, training aids, and eco-friendly pet supplies, all actively seeking influencers in 2026."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do micro-influencers get PR packages from pet brands in 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Absolutely! Many pet brands, especially those targeting specific niches, prioritize micro-influencers (10k-100k followers) in 2026 for their authentic engagement and dedicated audience, often sending PR packages."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should I include in my pitch to pet brands in 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Your pitch for 2026 should include an introduction, your audience demographics, engagement rates, content examples, why you\'re a good fit for their brand, and your media kit or collaboration ideas."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are there specific niches within pet influencing that are growing in 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, niches like sustainable pet products, pet tech, raw or gourmet pet food, and content focused on specific breeds or pet health issues are seeing significant growth in 2026, offering unique collaboration opportunities."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What makes a pet influencer attractive to brands in 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Brands in 2026 look for authentic engagement, high-quality visuals, a clear niche, consistent posting, and a professional approach to collaborations. A genuine passion for pets is also key."}}]},"image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1556740758-90de374c12ad?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=1170&q=80"}}')}}]);